  "rulesSectionYourTurn": "Your Turn",
  "rulesObjectiveBody": "Be the last cat standing. Everyone else explodes (unless they defuse in time) until only one is left.",
  "rulesBeforeStartBody": "Each player starts with 7 cards and 1 Defuse. The rest of the deck (with enough Exploding Kittens to leave one fewer than the number of players) is shuffled and dealt face down in the middle.",
  "rulesYourTurnBody": "You can play as many action cards as you want, or none at all. When you're done, you always have to draw a card from the deck to end your turn. If you draw an Exploding Kitten and don't have a Defuse, you're eliminated on the spot.",
  "rulesExplodingKittenDesc": "If you draw it and don't have a Defuse, you're eliminated. It's not played from your hand: it only shows up when you draw it.",
  "rulesDefuseDesc": "Saves you from an Exploding Kitten: you hide it back in the deck, wherever you choose.",
  "rulesNopeDesc": "Cancels the last card played (except an Exploding Kitten or a Defuse). Anyone can play it, at any time, even if it's not their turn — even to cancel another Nope.",
  "rulesAttackDesc": "Ends your turn without drawing, and the next player has to take two turns in a row.",
  "rulesSkipDesc": "Ends your turn without drawing. Careful: if you were attacked and owe two turns, a Skip only clears one — you still need to play or draw once more.",
  "rulesFavorDesc": "Pick another player and they have to give you a card from their hand — they choose which one, not you.",
  "rulesShuffleDesc": "Reshuffles the deck at random. No one sees the cards.",
  "rulesSeeTheFutureDesc": "You look at the top 3 cards of the deck, in order, without changing anything.",
  "rulesCatNeedsPairDesc": "Does nothing on its own — it needs a pair.",
  "rulesCatExplainerIntro": "No single cat card does anything on its own: they're \"junk cards\" that only work combined.",
  "rulesCatExplainerPairTrio": "Combine 2 matching cats to pick another player and steal a random card from their hand. With 3 matching, you choose which card to steal, but blind: you see their hand face down and tap a position without knowing what it is until you get it.",
  "rulesCatExplainerLeftover": "If you're left with only unpaired cats, no worries: you can't play them, so just tap the deck to draw and keep going.",

